1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,669
Prepare your chart before price gets there.

2
00:00:03,050 --> 00:00:05,946
Every report comes with the
zone and its key levels.

3
00:00:05,946 --> 00:00:07,616
Copy them from your dashboard.

4
00:00:07,816 --> 00:00:09,990
Mark the zone with its two prices.

5
00:00:10,316 --> 00:00:13,316
Add the key levels. That's
where the reaction can start.

6
00:00:13,516 --> 00:00:16,470
Set an alert on the edge price reaches first.

7
00:00:16,470 --> 00:00:20,802
FXMM doesn't notify you when price
gets there. Your platform does.

8
00:00:21,002 --> 00:00:24,263
No need to watch the screen all
day. The alert will tell you.

9
00:00:24,567 --> 00:00:27,105
Each level on your chart
is there for a reason.

10
00:00:27,267 --> 00:00:30,232
The two edges show where the
zone starts and where it ends.

11
00:00:30,367 --> 00:00:33,673
The key levels show where a
reaction is more likely to start.

12
00:00:33,767 --> 00:00:39,697
They come from institutional data: a CME volume
node, an options cluster, or the gamma flip.

13
00:00:39,867 --> 00:00:45,221
So when the alert goes off, you're not starting
from zero. Everything is already on your chart.

14
00:00:45,417 --> 00:00:47,827
All that's left is to wait for a rejection.

